<h3 id="illi1">Any Illicit Drug Use</h3>

<p>Among people aged 12 or older in 2023, 24.9&nbsp;percent (or 70.5&nbsp;million people) used illicit drugs in the past year (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig12">Figures 12</a></span> and <span class="bold"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig13">13</a></span> and <span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#taba.5b">Table A.5B</a></span>). The percentage was highest among young adults aged 18 to 25 (39.0&nbsp;percent or 13.3&nbsp;million people), followed by adults aged 26 or older (23.9&nbsp;percent or 53.5&nbsp;million people), then by adolescents aged 12 to 17 (14.7&nbsp;percent or 3.8&nbsp;million people).</p>


