<h3 class="f100">By Race/Ethnicity</h3>

<p>The percentage of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used illicit drugs in the past year was higher among American Indian or Alaska Native (36.7&nbsp;percent) or Multiracial people (36.2&nbsp;percent) than among White (26.1&nbsp;percent), Hispanic (21.6&nbsp;percent), or Asian people (12.4&nbsp;percent) (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig14">Figure 14</a></span> and <span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#tabb.8b">Table B.8B</a></span>). The percentage also was higher among Multiracial people than among Black people (27.7&nbsp;percent). Black or White people were more likely to have used illicit drugs in the past year compared with Hispanic people.</p>


