</figure>


<h3 id="init1">Initiation of Nicotine Vaping</h3>

<p>Among people aged 12 or older in 2023, 5.9&nbsp;million people initiated nicotine vaping in the past year, meaning they had never vaped nicotine before the past 12&nbsp;months (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig25">Figures 25</a></span> and <span class="bold"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig26">26</a></span> and <span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#taba.13a">Table A.13A</a></span>). Approximately half of all people who initiated nicotine vaping in the past year were aged 26 or older. In 2023, 1.5&nbsp;million&nbsp;adolescents aged 12 to 17, 1.4&nbsp;million young adults aged 18 to 25, and 3.1&nbsp;million adults aged 26 or older initiated nicotine vaping in the past year. About two thirds (62.5&nbsp;percent) of the 5.9&nbsp;million people in 2023 who initiated nicotine vaping in the past year did so at age 21 or older (3.7&nbsp;million people) compared with 37.5&nbsp;percent (or 2.2&nbsp;million people) who did so before age 21 (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig27">Figure 27</a></span> and <span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#taba.14ab">Table A.14AB</a></span>).</p>


