<h3 class="f100">By Race/Ethnicity</h3>

<p>Percentages of adolescents aged 12 to 17 in 2023 who had a past year MDE were higher among Multiracial (24.4&nbsp;percent) or White adolescents (19.6&nbsp;percent) compared with Asian (13.7&nbsp;percent) or Black adolescents (13.3&nbsp;percent) (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig37">Figure 37</a></span> and <span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#tabb.15b">Table B.15B</a></span>). Hispanic adolescents (18.0&nbsp;percent) were more likely to have had a past year MDE compared with Black adolescents. Estimates for a past year MDE could not be calculated with sufficient precision for American Indian or Alaska Native adolescents or Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander adolescents.<sup><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#end15">15</a></sup></p>


