</figure>

<h3 class="f100">By Race/Ethnicity</h3>

<p>Among adults aged 18 or older in 2023, Multiracial adults (36.7&nbsp;percent) were more likely to have had AMI in the past year compared with White (24.0&nbsp;percent), American Indian or Alaska Native (23.5&nbsp;percent), Hispanic (20.6&nbsp;percent), Black (19.4&nbsp;percent), or Asian adults (18.1&nbsp;percent) (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig40">Figure 40</a></span> and <span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#tabb.17b">Table B.17B</a></span>). The percentage of adults with AMI in the past year was also higher among White adults than among Hispanic, Black, or Asian adults. The estimate of AMI in the past year could not be calculated with sufficient precision for Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander adults.<sup><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#end15">15</a></sup></p>


