<p>Among the 5.1&nbsp;million adults aged 18 or older in 2023 with coâ€‘occurring SMI and an SUD who received either substance use treatment or mental health treatment in the past year (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig64">Figure 64</a></span>), most received only mental health treatment (63.0&nbsp;percent).<sup><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#end24">24</a></sup> An estimated 3.1&nbsp;percent of these adults aged 18 or older received only substance use treatment, and 33.9&nbsp;percent received both types of treatment.<sup><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#end24">24</a></sup></p>

<p>Among adults aged 18 or older in 2023 with coâ€‘occurring SMI and an SUD in the past year, young adults aged 18 to 25 were less likely than adults aged 26 to 49 to have received either substance use treatment or mental health treatment in the past year (<span class="bold nowrap"><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#taba.48b">Table A.48B</a></span>). Specifically, 67.0&nbsp;percent of young adults aged 18 to 25 with coâ€‘occurring SMI and an SUD in the past year (or 1.2&nbsp;million people) received either substance use treatment or mental health treatment in the past year compared with 78.3&nbsp;percent of adults aged 26 to 49 with coâ€‘occurring SMI and an SUD in the past year (or 3.2&nbsp;million people). Percentages could not be calculated with sufficient precision for adults aged 50 or older with coâ€‘occurring SMI and an SUD in the past year.<sup><a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#end15">15</a></sup></p>
