<section class="notes">
<h3 class="endnotes2">Long Descriptions â€“ Figures</h3>

<p id="fig1desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;1.</span> Figure&nbsp;1 is a horizontal bar graph, where the number of past month users in&nbsp;millions is shown on the horizontal axis, and 12 substance use or misuse categories are shown on the vertical axis.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used alcohol in the past month was 134.7&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used tobacco products in the past month was 49.9&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who vaped nicotine in the past month was 26.6&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used marijuana in the past month was 43.6&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used hallucinogens in the past month was 2.6&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who misused prescription pain relievers in the past month was 2.2&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used cocaine in the past month was 1.8&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used methamphetamine in the past month was 1.6&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who misused prescription tranquilizers or sedatives in the past month was 1.2&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who misused prescription stimulants in the past month was 1.2&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used inhalants in the past month was 1.0&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used heroin in the past month was 376,000.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig1">Return to Figure&nbsp;1</a>.</p>

<p id="fig2desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;2.</span> Figure&nbsp;2 is a pie chart with an accompanying horizontal bar graph, where the pie chart shows the number and percentage of people who did not use a tobacco product or vape nicotine in the past month and the number and percentage of people who used a tobacco product or vaped nicotine in the past month. The bar graph breaks down the group of people who used a tobacco product or vaped nicotine in the past month by showing the number of past month users in&nbsp;millions on the horizontal axis. Four types of tobacco products (cigarettes, cigars, smokeless tobacco, and pipe tobacco) and nicotine vaping are shown on the vertical axis.<br>
For the pie chart, the number and percentage of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who did not use a tobacco product or vape nicotine in the past month were 219.1&nbsp;million people and 77.3&nbsp;percent, respectively. The number and percentage of people who used a tobacco product or vaped nicotine in the past month were 64.4&nbsp;million people and 22.7&nbsp;percent, respectively.<br>
For the bar graph, of the 64.4&nbsp;million people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used a tobacco product or vaped nicotine in the past month:<br>
The number of people who used cigarettes in the past month was 38.7&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people who used cigars in the past month was 10.7&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people who used smokeless tobacco in the past month was 7.0&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people who used pipe tobacco in the past month was 2.0&nbsp;million.<br>
The number of people who vaped nicotine in the past month was 26.6&nbsp;million.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig2">Return to Figure&nbsp;2</a>.</p>

<p id="fig3desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;3.</span> Figure&nbsp;3 is a stacked bar graph. The horizontal axis shows four age groups (12 or older, 12 to 17, 18 to 25, and 26 or older). The vertical axis shows the percentage of people who used nicotine products in the past month.<br>
Each age group contains one bar. Each bar is divided into three sections. The top section represents the percentage of people in that age group who used nicotine products in the past month and who vaped nicotine only. The middle section represents the percentage of people in that age group who used nicotine products in the past month and who vaped nicotine and used tobacco products. The bottom section represents the percentage of people in that age group who used nicotine products in the past month and who used tobacco products only.<br>
Among people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used nicotine products in the past month, 22.5&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine only, 18.8&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine and used tobacco products, and 58.7&nbsp;percent used tobacco products only.<br>
Among people aged 12 to 17 in 2023 who used nicotine products in the past month, 74.9&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine only, 16.5&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine and used tobacco products, and 8.6&nbsp;percent used tobacco products only.<br>
Among people aged 18 to 25 in 2023 who used nicotine products in the past month, 47.6&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine only, 32.8&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine and used tobacco products, and 19.6&nbsp;percent used tobacco products only.<br>
Among people aged 26 or older in 2023 who used nicotine products in the past month, 15.7&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine only, 16.1&nbsp;percent vaped nicotine and used tobacco products, and 68.2&nbsp;percent used tobacco products only.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig3">Return to Figure&nbsp;3</a>.</p>

<p id="fig4desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;4.</span> Figure&nbsp;4 is a horizontal bar graph. The vertical axis shows a category for all people aged 12 or older and seven racial or ethnic group categories for people aged 12 or older. Racial or ethnic group categories are shown on the vertical axis in descending order of the associated percentages. The horizontal axis shows the percentage of people in that category who used tobacco or vaped nicotine in the past month. Each percentage includes a bar with the associated 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval.<br>
The percentage of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 22.7&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 21.9 to 23.6&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic American Indian or Alaska Native people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 34.0&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 26.1 to 43.0&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic Multiracial people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 30.6&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 26.1 to 35.5&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic White people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 24.7&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 23.6 to 25.9&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic Black people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 24.2&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 22.1 to 26.5&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Hispanic people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 17.9&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 16.1 to 19.8&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic Asian people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month was 10.3&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 8.1 to 13.0&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander people who used tobacco products or vaped nicotine in the past month is not shown due to low precision.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig4">Return to Figure&nbsp;4</a>.</p>

<p id="fig5desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;5.</span> Figure&nbsp;5 is a bar graph, where the horizontal axis shows four age groups (12 or older, 12 to 17, 18 to 25, and 26 or older). The vertical axis shows the percentage of people who used cigarettes in the past month.<br>
The percentage of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who used cigarettes in the past month was 13.7&nbsp;percent.<br>
The percentage of people aged 12 to 17 in 2023 who used cigarettes in the past month was 1.3&nbsp;percent.<br>
The percentage of people aged 18 to 25 in 2023 who used cigarettes in the past month was 10.6&nbsp;percent.<br>
The percentage of people aged 26 or older in 2023 who used cigarettes in the past month was 15.5&nbsp;percent.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig5">Return to Figure&nbsp;5</a>.</p>

<p id="fig6desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;6.</span> Figure&nbsp;6 is a bar graph, where the horizontal axis shows four age groups (12 or older, 12 to 17, 18 to 25, and 26 or older). The vertical axis shows the percentage of people who vaped nicotine in the past month.<br>
The percentage of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who vaped nicotine in the past month was 9.4&nbsp;percent.<br>
The percentage of people aged 12 to 17 in 2023 who vaped nicotine in the past month was 6.8&nbsp;percent.<br>
The percentage of people aged 18 to 25 in 2023 who vaped nicotine in the past month was 24.1&nbsp;percent.<br>
The percentage of people aged 26 or older in 2023 who vaped nicotine in the past month was 7.4&nbsp;percent.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig6">Return to Figure&nbsp;6</a>.</p>

<p id="fig7desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;7.</span> Figure&nbsp;7 is a three-circle diagram, where the smallest inner circle represents the number of people in&nbsp;millions who were heavy alcohol users in the past month. The smallest inner circle for heavy alcohol users is entirely inside of the second smallest inner circle, which represents the number of people in millions who were binge alcohol users in the past month. The second smallest inner circle for binge alcohol users is entirely inside of the largest circle, which represents the number of people in&nbsp;millions who were past month alcohol users. Thus, all heavy alcohol users are both binge alcohol users and past month alcohol users, and all binge alcohol users are past month alcohol users. In addition, the area within the second smallest inner circle but outside of the smallest inner circle represents people who were binge alcohol users but not heavy alcohol users in the past month. Also, the area within the largest circle but outside the second smallest inner circle represents people who were past month alcohol users but not binge alcohol users.<br>
Of the 134.7&nbsp;million people aged 12 or older in 2023 who were alcohol users in the past month, 61.4&nbsp;million were binge alcohol users, who made up 45.6&nbsp;percent of all past month alcohol users. There were 16.4&nbsp;million people aged 12 or older who were heavy alcohol users, who made up 26.7&nbsp;percent of all binge alcohol users and 12.2&nbsp;percent of all past month alcohol users.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig7">Return to Figure&nbsp;7</a>.</p>

<p id="fig8desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;8.</span> Figure&nbsp;8 is a bar graph, where past month alcohol use, past month binge alcohol use, and past month heavy alcohol use are shown on the horizontal axis. The vertical axis shows the percentage of people who used alcohol in the past month. For each level of alcohol use, the figure shows four bars, one per each age group (12 or older, 12 to 17, 18 to 25, and 26 or older).<br>
Percentages of people in 2023 who used alcohol in the past month were 47.5&nbsp;percent for people aged 12 or older, 6.9&nbsp;percent for people aged 12 to 17, 49.6&nbsp;percent for people aged 18 to 25, and 51.9&nbsp;percent for people aged 26 or older.<br>
Percentages of people in 2023 who were binge alcohol users in the past month were 21.7&nbsp;percent for people aged 12 or older, 3.9&nbsp;percent for people aged 12 to 17, 28.7&nbsp;percent for people aged 18 to 25, and 22.7&nbsp;percent for people aged 26 or older.<br>
Percentages of people in 2023 who were heavy alcohol users in the past month were 5.8&nbsp;percent for people aged 12 or older, 0.5&nbsp;percent for people aged 12 to 17, 6.9&nbsp;percent for people aged 18 to 25, and 6.2&nbsp;percent for people aged 26 or older.<br>
Long description end. <a href="https://www.samhsa.gov/data/sites/default/files/reports/rpt47095/National%20Report/National%20Report/2023-nsduh-annual-national.htm#fig8">Return to Figure&nbsp;8</a>.</p>

<p id="fig9desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;9.</span> Figure&nbsp;9 is a horizontal bar graph. The vertical axis shows a category for all people aged 12 or older and seven racial or ethnic group categories for people aged 12 or older. Racial or ethnic group categories are shown on the vertical axis in descending order of the associated percentages. The horizontal axis shows the percentage of people in that category who were binge alcohol users in the past month. Each percentage includes a bar with the associated 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval.<br>
The percentage of people aged 12 or older in 2023 who were binge alcohol users in the past month was 21.7&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 20.9 to 22.5&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Hispanic people who were binge alcohol users in the past month was 22.9&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 21.0 to 24.9&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic White people who were binge alcohol users in the past month was 22.4&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 21.5 to 23.4&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic Multiracial people who were binge alcohol users in the past month was 22.2&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 18.4 to 26.6&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic Black people who were binge alcohol users in the past month was 21.6&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 19.7 to 23.7&nbsp;percent).<br>
The percentage of Not Hispanic American Indian or Alaska Native people who were binge alcohol users in the past month was 19.1&nbsp;percent (with a 99&nbsp;percent confidence interval of 13.5 to 26.4&nbsp;percent).<br>
