<p id="fig23desc" class="endnotes2"><span class="bold nowrap">Figure&nbsp;23.</span> Figure&nbsp;23 is a Venn diagram with a label below the diagram that says, â€œ8.9 Million People Aged 12 or Older with Past Year Opioid Misuse.â€ The Venn diagram shows overlapping circles, with the circle on the top being much smaller than the circle on the bottom. The larger circle on the bottom represents people who were past year prescription pain reliever misusers. The much smaller circle on the top represents people who were past year heroin users. The intersection of the two circles represents people who were past year prescription pain reliever misusers and heroin users. The area of the larger circle that does not intersect with the smaller circle represents people who were past year prescription pain reliever misusers but not heroin users. The area of the smaller circle that does not intersect with the larger circle represents people who were past year heroin users but not prescription pain reliever misusers.<br>
